<title>FRANCE: SGS-Thomson falls over five percent.</title>
<headline>SGS-Thomson falls over five percent.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in SGS-Thomson Microelectronics NV fell by more than five percent in Paris after the company said it expected a delay in the recovery of the semiconductor market.</p>
<p>Earlier the company had announced a record 1996 net earnings figure, up 19 percent, but the fourth quarter was down and the company issued a warning for the first quarter.</p>
<p>At 1114 GMT, SGS-Thomson was down 5.57 percent at 407.00 francs.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
